<title>USA: Saliva Home Access Health drop lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Saliva Home Access Health drop lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER, Wash. 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saliva Diagnostic Systems Inc and Home Access Health Corp said they dropped a pending lawsuit and renegotited a contract.</p>
<p>Under the new contract, Saliva Diagnostics will license to Home Access its Omni-SAL, a saliva collection device used overseas in HIV testing.</p>
<p>Saliva Diagnostic will continue to sell and license Omni-SAL for rapid testing, for non-HIV applications and for HIV non-rapid testing other than for use in kits. Its license to Home Access applies only Home Access kits and only for non-rapid testing.</p>
</text>
